>Chastang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gajdos</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Severe community-acquired pneumonia. Etiology, epidemiology, and prognosis factors. French Study Group for Community-Acquired Pneumonia in the Intensive Care Unit</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1994</year><volume>105</volume><fpage>1487</fpage><lpage>1495</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8181342</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1378/chest.105.5.1487</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leroy</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Saux</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bedos</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Caulin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of lev-ofloxacin and cefotaxime combined with ofloxacin for ICU patients with community-acquired pneumonia who do not require vasopressors</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>2005</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>172</fpage><lpage>183</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16002932</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1378/chest.128.1.172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Angus</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Marrie</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Obrosky</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Clermont</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dremsizov</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Coley</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fine</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapoor</surname><given-names>WN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Severe community-acquired pneumonia: use of intensive care services and evaluation of American and British Thoracic Society Diagnostic criteria</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>166</volume><fpage>717</fpage><lpage>723</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12204871</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1164/rccm.2102084</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feikin</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuchat</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolczak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrett</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefkowitz</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>McGeer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Farley</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vugia</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lexau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Stefonek</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Patterson</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Jorgensen</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mortality from invasive pneumococcal pneumonia in the era of antibiotic resistance, 1995&#x02013;1997</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>229</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10667183</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Center for Health Statistics</collab></person-group><article-title>Leading causes of death, 1900&#x02013;1998</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/nchs/fasta